{"type":"message","id":"ae6c85f9","parentId":"b3af5a59","timestamp":"2026-03-26T09:28:13.841Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user scanned the QR code but there's no conversation entry point in WeChat. This is a known limitation - this plugin uses WeChat through some kind of WebSocket mechanism. Let me think about what this plugin does and what the user experience is.\n\nLooking at the plugin description: \"WeCom-based remote control channel for OpenClaw\" - it's WeCom (企微) based, not pure WeChat. That might be the issue.\n\nAlso from the earlier search results, the plugin description mentioned it works through a \"微信小程序ClawChat\" - so it might require a specific mini-app or something to work.\n\nActually wait, let me re-read the search results more carefully. The @fengcch plugin says \"终端二维码扫码登录，全自动轮询完成\" - terminal QR code login, fully automatic polling.\n \nLooking at the GitHub repo results, there were two different plugins found - one that's macOS-only with native notifications and webhook support for receiving messages, and another that provides a mini-app called ClawChat for WeChat interactions. The fengcch plugin might be using a different approach than what the user is expecting.\n\nSince the status command references WeCom-based functionality, I should clarify whether this is actually a WeChat integration or if it's using WeCom as the backend channel. The user might need to use the ClawChat mini-app to access OpenClaw through WeChat, or there could be a separate configuration needed to get the conversation interface working properly.","thinkingSignature":"135db4b5daf63b2b44d3dcf1646b396a6ee07af4034bfccc0ce9362a7d3ee10e"},{"type":"text","text":"这个插件底层用的是**企业微信**通道，不是直接微信对话。扫码后可能还需要：\n\n1. **登录的是企业微信** — 你扫的是企业微信的码？\n2. **需要一个对话入口** — 插件可能需要在企业微信里找到 \"OpenClaw\" 或 \"WeChat Access\" 的机器人，然后跟它对话\n\n你扫完码之后，企业微信里有没有出现一个新的联系人或者机器人？\n\n另外，这个插件的体验可能跟你想象的不太一样 — 它接入的是**企业微信**（WeCom），不是普通微信。如果你希望直接在微信里对话，可能需要 ClawBot 那个官方方案