{"type":"message","id":"7ec1f92d","parentId":"7d9a701f","timestamp":"2026-03-26T09:39:19.728Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The system is currently running OpenClaw 2026.3.23-2 (according to the gateway), but the CLI shows 2026.3.24. The system has broken npm modules (ajv is missing) which prevents `openclaw update` from working. \n\nAlso, there's an issue - the system notice shows that ajv module is missing for the openclaw CLI, but the gateway is running fine. The broken ajv is preventing some CLI commands from working.\n\nLet me also note that the user might be asking about the WeChat plugin updates rather than OpenClaw itself. Let me try to check the GitHub releases.\n\nActually, the user asked about \"你最新的版本更新了什么？\" which means \"what did the latest version update?\" - they might be referring to the WeChat plugin we just installed, or OpenClaw itself. \n\nGiven that the user is communicating in Chinese, they're most likely asking about the OpenClaw system itself rather than the plugin. The version mismatch between the gateway (2026.3.23-2) and CLI (2026.3.24) suggests there might be an update available, but the broken npm modules are preventing me from checking the full changelog.","thinkingSignature":"0a27d06a733c0ea6c99ec54db209e92686b90eeba6987db83e54238b1498f255"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_xow8a7iuhs74_1","name":"web_fetch","arguments":{"url":"https://managemyclaw.com/blog/openclaw-update-march-2026/","maxChars":4000}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":85217,"output":305,"cacheRead":35714,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":121236,"cost":{"input":0.0255651,"output":0.000366,"cacheRead":0.00214284,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02807394}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774517944794,"responseId":"061431bb8303fee4b259f2b0c25c4c09"}}
